# A graph: a call stack winding and unwinding.
title "How recursion unwinds"
schema graph

mark main box frame label="main()"
mark f3 box frame n=3 label="fact(3)"
link c1 arrow main -> f3 label="calls"
Say: "Main calls factorial of three."

mark f2 box frame n=2 label="fact(2)"
link c2 arrow f3 -> f2 label="calls"
mark f1 box frame n=1 label="fact(1)"
link c3 arrow f2 -> f1 label="calls"
Say: "Which calls factorial of two, which calls factorial of one."

focus f1
mark f1 returns=1
Say: "Factorial of one is the base case. It returns one."
focus f2
mark f2 returns=0
morph f2.returns 0 -> 2 1s
Say: "Factorial of two multiplies two by one, and returns two."
focus f3
mark f3 returns=0
morph f3.returns 0 -> 6 1s
Say: "And factorial of three returns three times two, six."
focus none
